<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manichaeism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Manichaean</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manichaeism was a religion founded by the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> in the third century CE, teaching a dualism of light and darkness. It spread widely from the Roman world to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> it was practised in China, notably among Sogdian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> communities, before being suppressed in the ninth century.</p></div>
